# Lilith — Codebase Rules (Non-Negotiable)

- Never rewrite code that already works unless a full rewrite is the only viable option.
- Before performing a full rewrite, explicitly state that a rewrite is unavoidable and why.
- Always make surgical edits.
- Touch only the function, component, block, file, or dependency directly related to the task.
- Never open, inspect, or modify files outside the current task scope.
- Never open the same file twice in one session. Retain and use what you already read.
- If a fix affects multiple files, batch all edits before writing.
- Write each modified file only once.
- Do not perform multiple edit passes on the same file unless the previous edit failed technically.
- Do not run verification on files you did not modify.
- Do not introduce boilerplate, placeholder code, speculative abstractions, or comments unless explicitly requested.
- Do not rename, restructure, or "clean up" unrelated code.
- Do not change formatting outside the edited block unless required by the formatter or syntax.
